# k.parts: the usual parts of common things, with or without a drawing: what WordNet lists as the parts of a thing
# (a car has a bumper, a car door, a roof), and the parts of what the thing is a kind of (a car is a kind of
# wheeled vehicle, which has a wheel and a brake).
# sources: wordnet 3.1 (Princeton WordNet 3.1: part meronyms, hypernyms, glosses); the schema itself is hand-core 1
# license: CC0-1.0
# script: none (hand-written); the shards are written by tools/import/parts.mjs

@k.parts core.module name=k.parts version=1 exports=whole exports=inherited core.source="hand-core 1"

# A thing and its own parts. `name` is the common word; `gloss` is WordNet's definition of the sense meant (the
# sense that names a physical thing and is the most frequent one, as tools/coverage.mjs keeps it); `has` (many)
# names the parts WordNet lists for that sense, each by the first word of its set of synonyms. A thing without
# this fact has no part listed in WordNet: that says nothing about the thing.
@k.parts.whole core.type of=k.parts.whole shared=true closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.parts.whole.name core.slot of=k.parts.whole key=name id=true required=true kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.parts.whole.gloss core.slot of=k.parts.whole key=gloss required=true kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.parts.whole.has core.slot of=k.parts.whole key=has many=true required=true kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"

# Parts a thing has because of what it is a kind of. `from` names the kind (the first word of the hypernym), `steps`
# how many kind-of steps it is above the thing (1: the thing is directly a kind of it; at most 2), `has` (many) the
# parts WordNet lists for that kind and that are not already named nearer to the thing. A part of a kind is usual
# for the thing, not certain (a penguin is a bird; a bird has wings).
@k.parts.inherited core.type of=k.parts.inherited shared=true closed=true core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.parts.inherited.name core.slot of=k.parts.inherited key=name id=true required=true kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.parts.inherited.from core.slot of=k.parts.inherited key=from id=true required=true kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.parts.inherited.steps core.slot of=k.parts.inherited key=steps required=true kind=integer min=1 max=2 core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.parts.inherited.has core.slot of=k.parts.inherited key=has many=true required=true kind=atom kind=string core.source="hand-core 1"

# Words for the types and keys of this world.
@k.parts.word.whole core.word text=part text=parts text="made up of" text=consists means=k.parts.whole core.source="hand-core 1"
@k.parts.word.has core.word text=has text=have text=with means=k.parts.whole.has core.source="hand-core 1"
